<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43586" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭ-vīvus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>half-alive</i>, <i>half-dead</i>, <i>almost dead</i> (class.; syn.
			semianimis). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ibi hominem fumo excruciatum, semivivum
					reliquit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 17, § 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bibulum semivivum reliquerunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 7, 2, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Pis. 14, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Brev. Vit. 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 4, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Luc.
				10, 30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum erat reclamatum semivivis mercenariorum
					vocibus,</span>”
				<i>with half-expiring words</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 59, 126</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
